Return nullptr instead of false from a pointer-returning function.

AICOMM_DeployStructure returns AvHAIBuildableStructure*. Converting `false`
to a pointer is ill-formed since C++11 and rejected by GCC >= 7.

--- a/main/source/mod/AvHAICommander.cpp
+++ b/main/source/mod/AvHAICommander.cpp
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 	// Don't allow the commander to place a structure somewhere unreachable to marines
 	if (!UTIL_PointIsReachable(WelderProfile, AITAC_GetTeamStartingLocation(pBot->Player->GetTeam()), Location, max_player_use_reach)) 
 	{
-		return false;
+		return nullptr;
 	}
 
 	AvHMessageID StructureID = UTIL_StructureTypeToImpulseCommand(StructureToDeploy);
